{"id":"8bb65109c23d2b60","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-thm-fodor-theorem.md","title":"Fodor's Theorem","display":"thm-fodor-theorem — Fodor's Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-fodor-theorem","aliases":["58-thm-fodor-theorem"],"display":"thm-fodor-theorem — Fodor's Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-regular-cardinal]]","[[58-df-stationary]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-fodor-theorem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-fodor-theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-fodor-theorem — Fodor's Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"58-df-regular-cardinal\">58-df-regular-cardinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b802c3dd76418d95\" href=\"?note=b802c3dd76418d95\" title=\"58-df-stationary\">58-df-stationary</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explicit relation signatures used below: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\subseteq V^{1}\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\subseteq V^{1}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Stationary}\\subseteq V^{2}\">\\(\\operatorname{Stationary}\\subseteq V^{2}\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\\subseteq\\kappa\">\\(S\\subseteq\\kappa\\)</span> (stationary set)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)\">\\(\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> is a regular uncountable cardinal (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"58-df-regular-cardinal\">58-df-regular-cardinal</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> is the regular-cardinal predicate</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Stationary}\">\\(\\mathrm{Stationary}\\)</span> is the stationarity predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"b802c3dd76418d95\" href=\"?note=b802c3dd76418d95\" title=\"58-df-stationary\">58-df-stationary</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}fodor\\text{-}theorem} \\vdash \\omega&lt;\\kappa\\land\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)\\land\\forall\\xi\\in S\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(f(\\xi)&lt;\\xi)\\to\\exists\\alpha&lt;\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Stationary}(\\{\\xi\\in S:f(\\xi)=\\alpha\\},\\kappa)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}fodor\\text{-}theorem} \\vdash \\omega&lt;\\kappa\\land\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)\\land\\forall\\xi\\in S\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(f(\\xi)&lt;\\xi)\\to\\exists\\alpha&lt;\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Stationary}(\\{\\xi\\in S:f(\\xi)=\\alpha\\},\\kappa)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The regression condition is expanded pointwise, including the conventional exclusion of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0\">\\(0\\)</span>, and the uncountability assumption is explicit.</li>\n<li>Fodor's lemma: a regressive function on a stationary set is constant on a stationary subset.</li>\n<li>This is a fundamental result in set theory.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-regular-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-regular-cardinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-stationary","status":"resolved","id":"b802c3dd76418d95","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-stationary]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)$ (see [[58-df-function]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-regular-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\kappa$ is a regular uncountable cardinal (see [[58-df-regular-cardinal]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-stationary","status":"resolved","id":"b802c3dd76418d95","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Stationary}$ is the stationarity predicate from [[58-df-stationary]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\subseteq V^{1}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Stationary}\\subseteq V^{2}","display":false},{"tex":"S\\subseteq\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Stationary}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}fodor\\text{-}theorem} \\vdash \\omega<\\kappa\\land\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)\\land\\forall\\xi\\in S\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(f(\\xi)<\\xi)\\to\\exists\\alpha<\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Stationary}(\\{\\xi\\in S:f(\\xi)=\\alpha\\},\\kappa)","display":true},{"tex":"0","display":false}],"bytes":1476,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4154","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-thm-fodor-theorem.md|58-thm-fodor-theorem]]（batch19）"}],"outgoing":["0fbfc19800246e77","b802c3dd76418d95","36d7463d215be751"]}